    {
      "id": "integrations.credential-file",
      "state": "Every credential and index file of the Linear, Jira and Bitbucket integrations: Linear workspace tokens (linear-tokens/<id>.enc) and the legacy linear-token.enc, the Linear workspace list (linear-workspaces.json), Jira site tokens (jira-tokens/<id>.enc) and the Jira site list (jira-sites.json), and the Bitbucket secret and metadata (bitbucket-credential.enc/.json). Tokens are safeStorage-encrypted where a keyring exists, else 0600 plaintext",
      "writer": "src/main/integration-credential-file.ts",
      "tier": "crash-durable",
      "lostIf": "The user is silently signed out of the integration and must re-authenticate. An empty token file reads as 'missing' and an empty workspace or site list reads as 'no workspaces' / 'no sites' by design, so a torn or truncated publish degrades straight to logged-out with no error.",
      "onFailure": "A failed save never touches the previous file. Every file of the population is published by the one writer: a 0600 temp sibling, short-write loop, fsync, close, rename; on any failure the temp is closed and removed, so the live token or list stays byte-identical and a fresh read returns the previous credential. Until 2026-10-04 the Linear and Jira token files and both index files were written in place with writeFileSync, which truncates on open, so a full disk emptied the working token before failing (measured RED). The save throws the OS error with its code intact (ENOSPC); the Linear token cache and both index caches (the Linear workspace list, the Jira site list) are assigned only after the write returns, so a failed save or rewrite does not advance memory past the disk, proven on the same module instance. Linear connect and test-connection, and Jira connect, catch it and return {ok:false} carrying the raw OS message, which the key and site dialogs render verbatim; the Bitbucket connect and the disconnect or select paths (Linear selectWorkspace, Jira selectSite and disconnect) do not catch, so the IPC call rejects with the raw error. Weaknesses stated, not fixed here: that raw text is what the user sees; Linear testConnection re-saves the stored token, so it is now safe on a full disk but still reports the OS text; Jira saves the token before the site list, so a failed list write leaves the new token with the old list while the user is told the connect failed. Proven by src/main/integration-token-save-disk-full.test.ts (injected ENOSPC modelled at the fs boundary with firing proof, for the Linear workspace and legacy tokens, the Jira token, both index files and the Bitbucket secret control, the same-instance index cases, and fsync-before-rename at the Linear and Jira token callers) and src/main/integration-credential-durability.test.ts at the primitive.",
